"BWIGLEY" <bwigley@xtra.co.nz> wrote:
>IIRC, if the polymorph doesn't put you in a tricky situation it
>doesn't get cured.

Prayer will not cure polymorph in the general case.  It treats
lycanthropy as a major trouble.

Furthermore, if you are lawful, and 90% of the time if you are neutral,
praying while polymorphed into an undead monster will result in you
being tagged with rehumanize() even if you are wearing an amulet of
unchanging.  This effect will work regardless of your prayer timeout.
It also works "safely" even when you are in Gehennom, because the
rehumanisation-of-the-undead path through prayer_done() returns, and
the check for rehumanisation happens *before* the check for being in
Gehennom.

On a side note: characters polyselfed into demons (monsters with the
M2_DEMON flag) are incapable of bringing themselves to utter a prayer
to a lawful or neutral god under any circumstances.  This applies
even if the type of demon into which you've been polymorphed is lawful.
